From 82478258d00d3b63673afca812817ebe337342a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:07:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: take the node's decoding and TxId of raw V2 txs in
 validate-tx

validate-tx and the broadcast token checks decoded raw txs with the
legacy TxMut::deser. A native V2 (v7) tx starts with a u64 lock and u16
input/output counts, which that decoder reads as an empty legacy tx, so
every V2 tx had no inputs or outputs, and lookup_spent_coins then
recomputed the txid of those empty legacy fields: one constant txid for
all V2 txs.

The new bridge call decode_raw_tx decodes the raw bytes with the node
and takes its inputs (mint inputs skipped, as indexed), outputs and
GetId, leaving the coins for lookup_spent_coins. Bytes the node cannot
decode keep their legacy fields and get the node txid of those fields.
lookup_spent_coins now only looks up coins and keeps the txid.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/035)
---
